.\" Man page for sniptext
.TH SNIPTEXT 1 "2025" "sniptext" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sniptext \- screen-capture OCR utility with adaptive ensemble recognition
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sniptext
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sniptext
captures a screen region, runs OCR on it, and copies the recognised text to
the clipboard.
In its default mode it starts a daemon that listens for a global hotkey.
Single-shot capture is available via \fB\-\-capture\-now\fR; processing an
existing image file via \fB\-\-file\fR.
.PP
Three OCR backends are supported: \fBtesseract\fR (fast, lightweight),
\fBeasyocr\fR (higher accuracy), and \fBensemble\fR (default — runs both and
merges results).  The adaptive mode (enabled by default) automatically selects
the fastest strategy based on image quality.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable debug logging to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-c " \fIFILE\fR, " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Path to a YAML configuration file.
Default: \fI~/.config/sniptext/config.yaml\fR.
.SS Capture modes (mutually exclusive)
.TP
.B \-\-capture\-now
Capture a screen region immediately (select with the mouse) without waiting
for the hotkey.  Useful from keyboard shortcuts in your window manager.
.TP
.BR \-\-file " \fIIMAGE\fR"
Run OCR on an existing image file instead of capturing the screen.
Supports any format that Pillow can open (PNG, JPEG, BMP, TIFF, …).
.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the recognised text to \fIFILE\fR in addition to copying it to the
clipboard.  Only valid with \fB\-\-capture\-now\fR or \fB\-\-file\fR.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Show an interactive preview of the OCR result in the terminal.  Allows
reviewing and editing the text before copying to clipboard.

.SS OCR
.TP
.BR \-\-ocr\-engine " \fIENGINE\fR"
Override the OCR engine for this run.  One of \fBtesseract\fR,
\fBeasyocr\fR, \fBensemble\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-models
List available OCR backends and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-benchmark " \fIIMAGE\fR"
Benchmark all available OCR engines on an image file and show timing results.
Useful for identifying the fastest engine for your workflow.

.SS History
.TP
.BR \-\-history " [\fIN\fR]"
Print the last \fIN\fR captured texts from history (default: 10) and exit.
Each entry is printed with its UTC timestamp.
.SS Daemon
.TP
.B serve
Start sniptext in daemon mode.  Keeps OCR models in memory for faster
subsequent captures.  Useful on Wayland systems with high OCR latency.
.TP
.BR \-\-client
Connect to a running daemon (started with \fBsniptext serve\fR) for capture
instead of running OCR locally.
.TP
.BR \-\-port " \fIPORT\fR"
Port for daemon server (default: 9877).  Only used with \fBserve\fR command.

.SS Configuration
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Print the current configuration in YAML format with inline comments and exit.
Useful for inspecting active settings or creating a config file template.
.TP
.BR \-\-profile " \fINAME\fR"
Load a named profile from
\fI~/.config/sniptext/profiles/NAME.yaml\fR and merge its values on top of
the base configuration.  Only the fields you wish to override need to be
present in the profile file.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-profiles
List available profiles (YAML files in
\fI~/.config/sniptext/profiles/\fR) and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is a YAML document located at
\fI~/.config/sniptext/config.yaml\fR by default.  Run
\fBsniptext \-\-print\-config\fR to see all available fields with their
current values and explanatory comments.
.PP
Key settings:
.TP
.B hotkey
Global hotkey that triggers a capture in daemon mode.  Default:
\fI<ctrl>+<alt>+t\fR.
.TP
.B ocr_engine
Backend to use: \fBensemble\fR (default), \fBtesseract\fR, or
\fBeasyocr\fR.
.TP
.B ocr_language
Tesseract language code(s).  For multiple languages use \fB+\fR as
separator, e.g. \fIeng+rus\fR.  EasyOCR language codes are derived
automatically.
.TP
.B ocr_confidence_threshold
Minimum confidence score (0.0–1.0) to accept an OCR result.
Default: \fI0.6\fR.
.TP
.B history_enabled " / " history_size
Enable or disable the capture history log and set the maximum number of
entries to keep.  Defaults: \fItrue\fR / \fI50\fR.
.TP
.B notification_enabled
Show a desktop notification after each successful capture.
Default: \fItrue\fR.
.SS Profiles
Create partial YAML files in \fI~/.config/sniptext/profiles/\fR to
define named configuration presets.  Only the fields you want to
override need to be listed.
.PP
Example — \fI~/.config/sniptext/profiles/fast.yaml\fR:
.PP
.nf
    ocr_engine: tesseract
    ocr_confidence_threshold: 0.5
.fi
.PP
Activate with: \fBsniptext \-\-profile fast \-\-capture\-now\fR
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sniptext/config.yaml
Main configuration file.  Created automatically on first run with commented
defaults.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sniptext/profiles/
Directory for named configuration profiles.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/sniptext/history.jsonl
Capture history log (one JSON object per line).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/sniptext/models/
Default directory for EasyOCR model files.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start in daemon mode (uses configured hotkey):
.PP
.nf
    sniptext
.fi
.PP
Capture a region immediately and copy to clipboard:
.PP
.nf
    sniptext \-\-capture\-now
.fi
.PP
Review and edit OCR result before copying:
.PP
.nf
    sniptext \-\-capture\-now \-\-interactive
.fi
.PP
Benchmark OCR engines on an image:
.PP
.nf
    sniptext \-\-benchmark screenshot.png
.fi
.PP
Start daemon server for faster Wayland captures:
.PP
.nf
    sniptext serve
    sniptext \-\-capture\-now \-\-client
.fi
.PP
Run OCR on an existing file and save the result:
.PP
.nf
    sniptext \-\-file screenshot.png \-\-output result.txt
.fi
.PP
Use the fast profile for a one-shot capture:
.PP
.nf
    sniptext \-\-profile fast \-\-capture\-now
.fi
.PP
Show the last 20 captured texts:
.PP
.nf
    sniptext \-\-history 20
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tesseract (1),
.BR notify-send (1),
.BR xclip (1),
.BR wl-copy (1)
